1
00:03:37,777 --> 00:03:43,777
Every love story begins with a kiss...

2
00:07:15,555 --> 00:07:21,555
The Princess and the Frog is a animation, romance,
fantasy film directed by Ron Clements.

3
00:10:53,333 --> 00:10:59,333
A waitress, desperate to fulfill her dreams as a restaurant owner, is set on a journey to turn a frog
prince back into a human being, but she has to face the same problem after she kisses him.

4
00:14:31,111 --> 00:14:37,111
Tiana (voice), played by Anika Noni Rose.

5
00:18:08,888 --> 00:18:14,888
Prince Naveen (voice), played by Bruno Campos.

6
00:21:46,666 --> 00:21:52,666
Ray (voice), played by Jim Cummings.

7
00:25:24,444 --> 00:25:30,444
Louis (voice), played by Michael-Leon Wooley.

8
00:29:02,222 --> 00:29:08,222
Dr. Facilier (voice), played by Keith David.

9
00:32:40,000 --> 00:32:46,000
Charlotte (voice), played by Jennifer Cody.

10
00:36:17,777 --> 00:36:23,777
The Princess and the Frog is a 2009 American animated musical fantasy
comedy film produced by Walt Disney Animation Studios.

11
00:39:55,555 --> 00:40:01,555
Inspired in part by the 2002 novel The Frog Princess by E.

12
00:43:33,333 --> 00:43:39,333
Baker, the story is a modern adaptation of the German folk tale
"The Frog Prince" as collected by the Brothers Grimm.

13
00:47:11,111 --> 00:47:17,111
The film was directed by John Musker and Ron Clements, and
written by Clements, Musker and Rob Edwards.

14
00:50:48,888 --> 00:50:54,888
It stars the voices of Anika Noni Rose, Bruno Campos, Michael-Leon Wooley, Jim Cummings, Jennifer Cody,
John Goodman, Keith David, Peter Bartlett, Jenifer Lewis, Oprah Winfrey, and Terrence Howard.

15
00:54:26,666 --> 00:54:32,666
Set in New Orleans during the 1920s, the film tells the story of a hardworking
waitress named Tiana who dreams of opening her own restaurant.

16
00:58:04,444 --> 00:58:10,444
After kissing prince Naveen, who has been turned into a frog by the evil voodoo witch doctor Facilier, Tiana
becomes a frog as well and the two must find a way to turn human again before it is too late.

17
01:01:42,222 --> 01:01:48,222
The Princess and the Frog began production in July 2006,
under the working title The Frog Princess.

18
01:05:20,000 --> 01:05:26,000
It marked Disney's brief return to traditional animation, as it was the mainstream animation
studio's first traditionally animated film since Home on the Range (2004).

19
01:08:57,777 --> 01:09:03,777
Musker and Clements, directors of Disney Animation's The Great Mouse Detective (1986), The Little Mermaid (1989), Aladdin
(1992), Hercules (1997), and Treasure Planet (2002) returned to Disney to direct The Princess and the Frog.

20
01:12:35,555 --> 01:12:41,555
The studio returned to a Broadway musical-style format frequently used during the Disney Renaissance, and the film features a score and songs
composed and conducted by Randy Newman, well known for his musical involvement in Pixar films such as the Toy Story franchise.

21
01:16:13,333 --> 01:16:19,333
The Princess and the Frog premiered at the Roy E.

22
01:19:51,111 --> 01:19:57,111
Disney Animation Building on the Walt Disney Studios lot in Burbank on November 15, 2009, and first opened in a
limited release in New York City and Los Angeles on November 25, followed by a wide release on December 11.

23
01:23:28,888 --> 01:23:34,888
The film received largely positive reviews from critics, who praised the return to a traditional hand-drawn animation style, though it was criticized for
its depiction of Louisiana Voodoo and alleged historical negationism of its depiction of the Southern United States during the Jim Crow era.

24
01:27:06,666 --> 01:27:12,666
Although it underperformed by Disney's standards, it grossed $271 million and received
three Oscar nominations: Best Animated Feature and two for Best Original Song.

25
01:30:44,444 --> 01:30:50,444
The film explores themes of princess, voodoo, new
orleans, louisiana, restaurant, villain.

26
01:34:22,222 --> 01:34:28,222
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
